# A1: the AUDITED eight-seat 262k attach of the whole stack on c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1-audit: the W1 profile plus every lever's audit - the drafter conv and heads audits (D2a, D2c, with the warm-pass fix: the served op and the audit clone compile in the warm pass),
# the unit-major reduce-scatter audit (U1, against the per-tile split), the host-gap full read-back audit of every staging destination (with the 1c shadow), and the fused-commit, verify-glue and draft-singles audits of the best-audit profile.
# The verify T1/T2 audits stay OFF (as in the host-gap audited arm): the shard audit would put the reference sampler back in the trace, and this arm carries the timed arm's sampler state (no in-trace sampler) but NOT its whole trace: U1's audited calls (3 reduce-scatters and 2 clones of each audited call, served from the split), the verify-glue clones and the D2 clones change it. (A) NOSAMP READ: there is NO "[PINDIAG] packed sampler arm" line in A1 (nosamp took effect); S0c's line shows in_trace=1.
# The smoke runs concurrent8_steady (the quad blocks' mix: the smoke rule needs it) and concurrent8_code_32k. READ in this order and stop at the first failure: (1) the attach: 'verify prestage two-block engaged' once for each block (mode=blocks),
# 'block epochs engaged blocks=2', 'tp4 u1 engaged' with unit_major above 0, 'tp4 draft conv engaged' and 'tp4 draft heads engaged', and NO refused or 'fell back' line of any of them (a [PINDIAG] tp4 u1 fell back line fails the smoke check);
# (2) ZERO audit mismatches of every kind: [PACKED-PRESTAGE-FULLAUDIT] (read apart by path, a path=diff line for each block), the D2 audit lines (exact), [PINDIAG] tp4 u1 audit ... exact=True with a replay (round>=1) line for each of the two block owners,
# the [DRAFT-SINGLES-AUDIT] equal=1 lines for both quad groups, the fused-commit and verify-glue audits; (3) c2_smoke_check clean; (4) every answer's content hash equal to S0c's on concurrent8_code_32k and concurrent8_code_equal.
# INTERACTION READ: the draft audits compare right after their own bucket's replay and the U1 audit right after its own block's replay (tile_collective_tp.audit_round refuses any other order): an 'audit was read after another block replayed' error is a capture-order finding, not a lever mismatch.
# U1 AUDIT COVERAGE: the U1 audit reads the first 32 of the 128 calls of a forward only; the other 96 rest on the answer hashes (the zero-mismatch read says nothing about them). D2 AUDIT ORDER: with two quads, quad A's audit compares at collect, after quad B's replay (compare_draft_audit has no replayed-owner guard): a D2 mismatch with exact clones elsewhere is first a capture-order finding. Then the stage 0 lines: [PACKED-HOSTGAP-WINDOW] (window_ms against fence_wait_ms). Duration (estimate): 180 min. Stop rule.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/w1 eight-seat 262k stack window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/w1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/w1 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-w1-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-w1-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_equal
